WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.623
Predicting where a street-view photo was taken is
useful for urban planning,

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:07.325
navigation, and social studies.

00:00:07.405 --> 00:00:11.028
But today's approaches have two blind spots.

00:00:11.108 --> 00:00:14.731
First,

00:00:14.811 --> 00:00:18.434
the data problem: street-view datasets are stuffed
with images captured in tunnels,

00:00:18.514 --> 00:00:22.136
against blank walls, or of generic vegetation,

00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:25.839
none of which contain clues a model could use to
locate them.

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:29.542
Second,

00:00:29.622 --> 00:00:33.245
the reasoning problem: retrieval and classification
models operate as black boxes,

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.947
handing back a coordinate with no explanation a
person could inspect or trust.

00:00:37.027 --> 00:00:40.650
This paper argues that both quality and
interpretability must be fixed together.
